@@ -16,3 +16,37 @@ Use the full finalizer annotation to supply those premises.
 This change adds no stored representation or machine behavior.
 Local configuration closure establishes neither history funding nor release custody.
 The finalizer endpoint still needs their composition.
+
+## Release custody at executable positions
+
+Concept: scope-lifetime-finalization R11.
+Question: release custody closes `FinalizerRun.once_placed_outside_census`.
+The full source balance already holds on every raw history.
+Its remaining premise bounds release-start production by earlier registrations.
+
+The old custody reading counts stored current code after parallel close has transferred its work.
+The parent stays running until an overwrite command executes.
+A command cut can discard that command, leaving the stored code unable to run.
+
+Use the existing fiber table and command list as the custody positions.
+Count current code in idle fibers and fibers owned by queued loop or delivery commands.
+Count saved frames, scope entries, dispatcher tasks, and unlaunched programs as before.
+Command ownership protects each untouched suffix.
+Dropping a command suffix can only reduce its current-code reservation.
+
+The generic split and installation laws belong beside `Machine.FiberSum`.
+Their consumer is the existing release-custody evaluator and command balance.
+The native case split stays in its existing producer.
+Only parallel close needs a new local transfer equation.
+The common decision lift carries the joined assertion.
+This route establishes no progress and adds no decision-admission premise.
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+  F[Existing fiber sum] --> A[Executable current-code reading]
+  A --> D[Existing native debit with parallel transfer]
+  D --> H[Common history lift]
+  H --> C[Release starts bounded by registration]
+  S[Full source funding] --> U[Once-placed registration bound]
+  C --> U
+```
